# Local Lead Finder — cron example (Linux / macOS).
#
# Install with:  crontab -e   (then paste a line below and save)
# List current:  crontab -l
#
# Replace /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/local-lead-finder with your repo path (run `pwd`).
# The wrapper resolves node + loads .env, so no secrets belong in the crontab.

# Every 4 hours, on the hour — one worker tick, appended to a log.
0 */4 * * * /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/local-lead-finder/deploy/run-worker.sh >> /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/local-lead-finder/worker.log 2>&1

# --- other cadences (pick ONE; a few times/day keeps you well under the cap) ---
# Twice a day (09:00 and 18:00):
# 0 9,18 * * * /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/local-lead-finder/deploy/run-worker.sh >> /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/local-lead-finder/worker.log 2>&1
# Every 6 hours:
# 0 */6 * * * /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/local-lead-finder/deploy/run-worker.sh >> /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/local-lead-finder/worker.log 2>&1
